[ar:ARK Music]
[ti:Do I Have to Earn It?]
[al:Problem's]

[00:02.15]Tell me what I owe you,
[00:04.38]Tell me what I missed,
[00:06.68]Tell me why a simple smile
[00:08.84]Feels harder than this.
[00:10.91]I learned to keep my hands clean,
[00:13.18]I learned to read the room,
[00:15.34]I learned that love gets quieter
[00:17.52]When you give it too soon.
[00:19.90]I knew the sound of footsteps
[00:21.75]Before they reached the door,
[00:23.86]Knew which kind of silence
[00:25.100]Meant I shouldn't ask for more.
[00:28.32]I kept my little victories
[00:30.54]Folded out of sight,
[00:32.52]Didn't want to make the morning
[00:34.07]Jealous of the night.
[00:36.87]I could change my colors,
[00:39.07]I could change my name,
[00:41.35]Could become the version
[00:43.40]That would never cause a flame.
[00:45.59]Every little “good job,”
[00:46.63]Every little “that's enough,”
[00:47.81]Felt like I was standing
[00:48.99]On a scale called love.
[00:50.94]So I ran for the answer,
[00:53.09]I chased every sign,
[00:55.10]Put a price on my heartbeat,
[00:57.24]Put a lock on my mind.
[00:59.40]Then somebody looked at me
[01:00.95]Like I didn't have to prove it,
[01:02.48]And for once I had no reason
[01:05.28]To know what to do with it.
[01:08.59]Do I have to earn it?
[01:10.62]Do I have to bleed?
[01:12.50]Do I have to become
[01:14.22]Everything you need?
[01:16.48]Do I have to win it?
[01:19.28]Do I have to change?
[01:21.08]Do I have to disappear
[01:23.21]To make somebody stay?
[01:25.54]If I fall, will you leave me?
[01:28.16]If I'm lost, will you see?
[01:29.39]If I bring you nothing,
[01:30.84]Will you still sit with me?
[01:33.96]Tell me, tell me honestly,
[01:36.36]Before I forget it:
[01:38.62]Do I have to earn it
[01:40.59]To be worth being loved?
[01:43.48]No, no, no,
[01:44.61]Don't make me count it anymore,
[01:47.01]No, no, no,
[01:48.98]I don't know what love was for.
[01:51.34]No, no, no,
[01:53.29]Maybe I can leave the door unlocked,
[01:55.41]Maybe I can stay here
[01:56.98]Without watching the clock.
[01:59.88]I saw the same old pattern
[02:01.42]Waiting in my hands,
[02:04.25]The words I swore I'd never say,
[02:06.17]The things I couldn't stand.
[02:08.50]Funny how a broken mirror
[02:10.64]Teaches you the frame,
[02:12.74]You start repeating echoes
[02:14.74]Then you wonder who's to blame.
[02:16.89]But somebody stayed quiet
[02:18.67]When I expected war,
[02:20.66]Left a little space beside them,
[02:22.87]Didn't ask me what it was for.
[02:25.12]No perfect little answer,
[02:27.24]No speech beneath the rain,
[02:29.33]Just a hand that didn't vanish
[02:31.42]When I showed a little pain.
[02:33.46]And I almost ran from kindness,
[02:35.89]Almost called it fake,
[02:37.84]Almost built another wall
[02:39.89]Before the wall could break.
[02:42.35]But something in that silence
[02:44.75]Felt different from before,
[02:46.53]Like maybe being wanted
[02:48.63]Didn't need a score.
[02:52.63]Do I have to earn it?
[02:54.39]Do I have to bleed?
[02:56.33]Do I have to become
[02:58.09]Everything you need?
[03:00.19]Do I have to win it?
[03:02.92]Do I have to change?
[03:04.84]Do I have to disappear
[03:06.69]To make somebody stay?
[03:08.89]If I fall, will you leave me?
[03:11.11]If I'm lost, will you see?
[03:13.11]If I bring you nothing,
[03:14.64]Will you still sit with me?
[03:17.34]Tell me, tell me honestly,
[03:19.64]Before I forget it:
[03:22.07]Do I have to earn it
[03:24.12]To be worth being loved?
[03:27.30]Maybe the hands that hurt you
[03:28.85]Don't get to hold your future.
[03:31.32]Maybe the voice that named you
[03:33.69]Doesn't get to name you now
[03:35.82]Maybe the house you came from
[03:38.07]Can end at your front door.
[03:40.16]Maybe you can break the pattern
[03:41.69]Without becoming what you hated.
[03:44.38]And maybe...
[03:45.34]You don't have to be useful
[03:46.80]To be held.
[03:47.50]You don't have to be perfect
[03:48.58]To be seen.
[03:49.73]You don't have to shrink
[03:50.78]To fit inside somebody's world.
[03:54.28]You can simply be here.
[03:55.73]No gold star,
[03:56.83]No perfect score,
[03:59.74]No running till your feet get sore.
[04:01.47]No changing shape,
[04:02.37]No closing eyes,
[04:03.37]No proving you deserve the light.
[04:10.27]Do I have to earn it?
[04:11.15]I don't think I do.
[04:13.70]Maybe all this running
[04:15.27]Wasn't leading me to you.
[04:18.38]I don't have to win it,
[04:29.68]I don't have to change,
[04:31.60]I don't have to disappear
[04:33.63]To make somebody stay.
[04:35.36]If I fall, you can see me,
[04:37.48]If I'm lost, I'll still breathe,
[04:39.77]If I bring you nothing,
[04:41.22]There's still room here for me.
[04:43.81]Tell me, tell me honestly,
[04:46.40]Now that I finally get it:
[04:48.55]I never had to earn it
[04:50.20]To be worth being loved.
[04:53.84]No, no, no,
[04:55.14]Leave the little tally on the floor,
[04:58.16]No, no, no,
[04:59.22]I don't need to count anymore.
[05:01.95]No, no, no,
[05:03.68]Let the old rules fade away,
[05:06.87]I can walk into tomorrow
[05:09.48]As I am today.
[05:12.06]Tell me what I owe you...
[05:14.07]Nothing.
[05:15.88]Tell me what I missed...
[05:16.61]Nothing.
[05:18.17]Tell me what I have to become...
[05:21.10]Nothing.
[05:22.85]Maybe that's the first thing
[05:25.47]I was never taught.